WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.920
Good morning Hank; it's Sunday, it's news day,

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:05.380
and today I'm going to discuss the rumored demise of the "You" in "YouTube."

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:14.400
But first, important messages for Nerdfighters in Philadelphia or Australia!

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:17.000
I'm going to be talking and signing copies of my books this Saturday

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.420
at the Philadelphia Book Festival at 3:30pm, more info in the sidebar –

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:25.300
and there's going to be an awesome nerdfightastic nerdfighter gathering on Sunday, May 31st

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:27.720
in Melbourne, Australia, featuring me!

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:29.500
Yay!

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:30.740
Australia!

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:33.440
So Hank, you might be wondering why I dressed up for my video today –

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:36.540
It's because I'm trying to make us more attractive to advertisers.

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:37.940
But I'm not wearing any pants.

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:40.260
You can't make me wear pants, advertisers!

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:44.940
Hank, it's been widely reported that this Thursday, YouTube is going to launch a major redesign of this site

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:48.900
that will emphasize professional content over user-generated content.

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:54.820
The reports say that there will now be four tabs: there will be TV, Movies, Music, and then Videos,

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:58.440
and then all of the user-generated content will be in that "Videos" tab.

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:03.020
And so the site will begin emphasizing more television shows, and feature-length movies, and music videos,

00:01:03.020 --> 00:01:05.720
not so much because that's what people want to watch,

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:08.700
but because that's what advertisers want to advertise next to.

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:12.360
And of course the entire Youtube community is going to be furious about this –

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:13.240
because, well,

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:17.040
first, because that's what the Youtube Community does – it gets furious.

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:20.580
And secondly they'll be furious because this new redesign hurts the little guy –

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:24.140
but it's strange to me that we think that YouTube has a responsibility to the little guy.

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:28.000
Corporations are not in the business of being awesome. They exist to make money,

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:32.980
and according to almost every analyst on Wall Street, YouTube loses money hand over fist!

00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:37.240
Because it turns out that tens of millions of people want to watch squirrels water-skiing for free,

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:39.400
but it's difficult to monetize those views

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:43.980
because Lucky Charms doesn't want to associate their brand with water-skiing squirrels.

00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:49.260
Advertisers want to be associated with, like, American Dad, and Bones.

00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:51.920
So for the number of views that it takes YouTube to make a dollar,

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:55.540
a site like Hulu, that features television shows, can make ten dollars.

00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:58.860
So Hank, I find it hard to get mad at YouTube for wanting to stop losing money.

00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:03.940
But I am a little bit mad at advertisers for thinking that user-generated content can't sell Lucky Charms.

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:06.100
I can sell Lucky Charms as well as anybody!

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:08.660
Lucky Charms are like the vampires of breakfast cereal:

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:12.820
They're magical, they're delicious, they're a little bit dangerous and bad for you,

00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:15.740
they initially make you feel great, but then over time you realize that

00:02:15.740 --> 00:02:19.140
maybe your relationship with Lucky Charms is just a little bit unhealthy,

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:22.080
and you start to think maybe I don't want to be in a long-term relationship

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:25.220
with a breakfast cereal that tastes delicious but damages my health.

00:02:25.220 --> 00:02:28.460
But then the Lucky Charms gets all stalker on you, and then for some reason you kinda like that,

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:32.220
it makes you feel special, so, yeah, you spend your life with Lucky Charms.

00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:35.400
That's...awesome, that's a great way to...get diabetes.

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:39.520
Aaaahhh, Hank, I can't sell Lucky Charms, it's just not in me!

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:44.160
So YouTubers, if you're gonna get mad, that's okay, but don't get mad at YouTube for wanting to make money.

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:47.560
Get mad at me for being so bad at selling Lucky Charms.

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:51.420
That said, Hank, there is one reported change coming to YouTube that makes me furious.

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:55.860
Reports are that YouTube will soon have a feature where you can dim all the space, like, out there,

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:57.220
outside of the video screen?

00:02:57.220 --> 00:02:58.320
And I hate that idea.

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:01.560
What I hate about television is that television is something you watch.

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:06.300
What I love about YouTube is that it's not television, it's something that you're called to participate in.

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:09.560
My favorite thing about YouTube isn't even what happens inside of here,

00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:11.760
my favorite thing is what happens down there!

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:17.580
(Uh, it looked like I was pointing at my pants, but I wasn't pointing at my pants, because I don't have pants on.)

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:19.140
I was pointing at the comments,

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:23.960
and admittedly the quality of discourse in many YouTube video comments leaves a little bit to be desired.

00:03:23.960 --> 00:03:29.780
But for our community, at least, the comments and video responses are a huge portion of what goes on in these videos.

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:34.400
And I hate the idea of making it possible to dim the screen around you so you can pretend you're watching television.

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:37.200
Hank? Nerdfighters? You're not watching anything.

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:40.720
Now let's continue this conversation down below.

